### ⚠️ APPROACH 1 (NOT RECOMMENDED): Calculate STOP LOSS PRICE for Fixed Lot Size
*(Only use if you have a FIXED lot size and MUST force 1% loss — rare edge case)*

```mql5
double CalculateSLByRisk(
    string symbol,
    ENUM_ORDER_TYPE order_type,
    double volume,      // FIXED lot size (e.g., 0.1)
    double entry_price,
    double risk_percent = 1.0
    )
{
    double balance = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE);
    double risk_amount = balance * (risk_percent / 100.0);

    double tick_size = SymbolInfoDouble(symbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_SIZE);
    if(tick_size <= 0) tick_size = SymbolInfoDouble(symbol, SYMBOL_POINT);

    double profit_tick = 0;
    bool calc_ok = false;

    if(order_type == ORDER_TYPE_BUY)
    {
        calc_ok = OrderCalcProfit(ORDER_TYPE_BUY, symbol, volume, entry_price, entry_price - tick_size, profit_tick);
        if(!calc_ok || profit_tick >= 0) return 0;
        double loss_per_tick = -profit_tick; // Positive value
        if(loss_per_tick <= 0) return 0;
        return entry_price - (risk_amount / loss_per_tick) * tick_size;
    }
    else // SELL
    {
        calc_ok = OrderCalcProfit(ORDER_TYPE_SELL, symbol, volume, entry_price, entry_price + tick_size, profit_tick);
        if(!calc_ok || profit_tick >= 0) return 0;
        double loss_per_tick = -profit_tick;
        if(loss_per_tick <= 0) return 0;
        return entry_price + (risk_amount / loss_per_tick) * tick_size;
    }
}
```
❗ **Why Avoid Approach 1?**  
- Stops placed illogically (ignoring price action) → higher chance of being hit by noise  
- Violates core risk management principles  
- May place SL inside spread or violate broker requirements  
- Balance changes between trades → inconsistent SL placement  

